{"name":"Braided Raffia","hex":"#e1d0af","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"braided","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of braid"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Plaited, woven, entwined.","Divided into several channels."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/braided"},{"term":"raffia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous material used for tying plants, originating from the leaves of raffia palm trees (genus Raphia)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raffia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Braided","blocks":[{"text":"Braided is a musical group consisting of Casey LeBlanc, Ashley Leitão, and Amber Fleury, who all competed on the third season of Canadian Idol in 2005. They are the third music group to come from an Idol show in the world, after Young Divas from Australia and Feminnem from Croatia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braided","wikidata":"Q4955648"},{"title":"Raffia palm","blocks":[{"text":"Raffia palms are members of the genus Raphia. The Malagasy name rafia is derived from fia \"to squeeze juice\". The genus contains about twenty species of palms native to tropical regions of Africa, and especially Madagascar, with one species also occurring in Central and South America. R. taedigera is the source of raffia fibers, which are the veins of the leaves, and this species produces a fruit called \"brazilia pods\", \"uxi nuts\" or \"uxi pods\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Raphia_australis.jpg/330px-Raphia_australis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raffia_palm","wikidata":"Q133289"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Making_raffia_rope.jpg/500px-Making_raffia_rope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com